  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two integers NNN and KKK. Find any two integers aaa and bbb such that\n\n\n1≤a,b≤N1 \\leq a, b \\leq N1≤a,b≤N,\n∣a−b∣≥K|a - b| \\geq K∣a−b∣≥K, and\n∣gcd⁡(a,b)−lcm(a,b)∣≥2K|\\gcd(a, b) - \\text{lcm}(a, b)| \\geq 2K∣gcd(a,b)−lcm(a,b)∣≥2K\nThat is, your task is to find any two integers not exceeding NNN, such that they differ by at least KKK and their GCD and LCM differ by at least 2K2K2K.\n\nIt is possible that no valid (a,b)(a, b)(a,b) exist, in which case you must print −1-1−1 twice instead.\n\nAs a reminder,\n\n\ngcd⁡(a,b)\\gcd(a, b)gcd(a,b) denotes the greatest common divisor of aaa and bbb.\nlcm(a,b)\\text{lcm}(a, b)lcm(a,b) denotes the least common multiple of aaa and bbb.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, on a new line:\n\n\n\nIf no valid pair exists, print the integer −1-1−1 twice, separated by a space.\nOtherwise, print the integers aaa and bbb you found, separated by a space. These two integers should satisfy all the conditions laid out in the statement.\n\nIf multiple valid pairs exist, you may find any of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N,K≤1091 \\leq N, K \\leq 10^91≤N,K≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n6 2\n10 6\n8 11\n7 1",
        "output": "4 6\n10 3\n-1 -1\n4 6",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Choosing a=4,b=6a = 4, b = 6a=4,b=6 gives ∣a−b∣=2|a - b| = 2∣a−b∣=2 and ∣gcd⁡(a,b)−lcm(a,b)∣=∣2−12∣=10|\\gcd(a, b) - \\text{lcm}(a, b)| = |2 - 12| = 10∣gcd(a,b)−lcm(a,b)∣=∣2−12∣=10.\nSince K=2K = 2K=2 here, 2≥K2 \\geq K2≥K and 10≥2K10 \\geq 2K10≥2K, so this pair of elements is valid.\nTest case 222: With a=10,b=3a = 10, b = 3a=10,b=3, we have ∣a−b∣=7≥K|a - b| = 7 \\geq K∣a−b∣=7≥K and ∣gcd⁡(a,b)−lcm(a,b)∣=29≥2K|\\gcd(a, b) - \\text{lcm}(a, b)| = 29 \\geq 2K∣gcd(a,b)−lcm(a,b)∣=29≥2K.\nTest case 333: It can be shown that no valid solution exists."
      }
    ]
